<title>CANADA: CP plans to buy back up to 18 mln shares.</title>
<headline>CP plans to buy back up to 18 mln shares.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Pacific Ltd said on Tuesday that it planned to buy back up to 18 million of its common shares, or about 5.3 percent of its 341.5 million shares outstanding.</p>
<p>The share purchases, which are subject to regulatory approvals, will begin on August 19, 1997 and end by August 18, 1998 and be made through the Toronto, Montreal, Vancouver, Alberta and New York Stock Exchanges.</p>
<p>CP said it purchased 1.7 million common shares under a normal course issuer bid within the past 12 months at an average price of C$34.86 a share.</p>
<p>CP shares rose 0.75 to 41 in Toronto today.</p>
<p>((Reuters Montreal bureau 514-985-2434))</p>
</text>
